.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt MASTER-FIX 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm /fix
.Nd inspect, repair and verify a repository target
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar path
.Nm
.Fl -dry-run
.Op Ar path
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Cm /fix
is the canonical repair operation inside the MASTER interactive session.
It inventories the target, evaluates findings against the active Laws, applies
admitted repairs, re-observes the result and verifies convergence.
.Pp
An unbounded repair must inventory the eligible corpus before dispatching
changes.
A bounded run proves only the work it actually selected.
.Cm --dry-run
requests a read-only preview; it must not change source files, Git state,
run journals or delivery state.
.Pp
The final report must preserve the real terminal outcome.
A plateau, human
decision, blocked operation, validation failure, delivery failure or timeout
is not a successful completion.
.Pp
.Fl -dry-run
reads without writing, and
.Fl -critique
convenes the council on that reading:
.Cm /fix
is the one command.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
MASTER/bin/master
/fix
/fix RAILS
/fix --dry-run MASTER
/fix --dry-run --critique RAILS
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr master 1 ,
.Xr operator 1
